Xiuqing and his followers are slaughtered on Hong Xiuquan’s orders</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/tanzimat"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzimat.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzimat</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Imperial Reform Edict promises full legal equality for citizens of all religions and abolishes the jizya</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/awadh-state"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Awadh%20State.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Awadh State</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lord Dalhousie deposes Wajid Ali Shah and annexes Oudh to the East India Company's territories</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/menelik-ii"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Menelik%20II.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Menelik II</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After fighting between Tewodros II and his father's Shewans, the boy is captured and taken to Tewodros's court at Maqdala</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/empress-dowager-cixi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empress%20Dowager%20Cixi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empress Dowager Cixi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">She gives birth to Zaichun, the Xianfeng Emperor's first and only surviving son</span></li></ul></section>
